# The C wide-character and multibyte functions, written in SemanticScript (D-153): wctype.h, the parts of wchar.h that need no formatted I/O, stdlib.h's multibyte functions, and uchar.h's, as glibc behaves in the C locale.
#
# This module is generated from tools/cwide.dsl by tools/build.py.

cwide is module
cwide purpose "The C wide-character and multibyte functions in SemanticScript: wctype.h's classes and cases, wchar.h's text without formatted I/O, stdlib.h's multibyte functions, and uchar.h's, as glibc behaves in the C locale (wchar_t is 32 bits)"
cwide path cwide
cwide imports standard.machine
cwide imports standard.string
cwide imports standard.math
cwide imports standard.compare
cwide imports standard.convert
cwide imports standard.bits
cwide imports standard.logic
cwide imports standard.test
cwide imports kernel
cwide imports memory
cwide imports heap
cwide imports bignum
cwide imports clibrary
cwide exports none

memoryAccess is capability
memoryAccess purpose "Authority to read and write the memory C callers hand the library"
memoryAccess grants use machine.memory none

systemCalls is capability
systemCalls purpose "Authority to take memory from the heap and to read the text wcstod reads"
systemCalls grants use system.calls none

# Every function here is an `abi library "<name>"` operation (D-153, D-155): the C calling convention under its C name.
# In the C locale glibc classifies and changes case for ASCII only, so codes outside 0 to 127 are in no class and
# keep their case. A wide character is 32 bits (wchar_t is int on Linux; on Windows it is kept 32 bits too). The
# C locale's multibyte encoding is ASCII, as glibc's is (D-177): the bytes 0 to 127 are the wide characters 0 to
# 127, a byte from 128 to 255 is an invalid sequence and a wide character past 127 has no byte (EILSEQ either way;
# btowc and wctob give WEOF and EOF). MB_CUR_MAX is 1.
# machine.state bytes 26624 to 26879 belong to this module: the tests' scratch text (which the library never reads).
wideSize is constant
wideSize purpose "sizeof(wchar_t): 4 bytes"
wideSize type Int64
wideSize value 4

forever is constant
forever purpose "The bound of a loop that ends by its own test"
forever type Int64
forever value 9223372036854775807

eilseqError is constant
eilseqError purpose "EILSEQ: a wide character with no byte in the C locale"
eilseqError type Int32
eilseqError value 84

scratchAt is constant
scratchAt purpose "Where the tests write their text, in machine.state"
scratchAt type Int64
scratchAt value 26624

singleInexactAt is constant
singleInexactAt purpose "Where nearestSingle says whether the float differs from the double, in machine.state"
singleInexactAt type Int64
singleInexactAt value 26864

rangeErrorNumber is constant
rangeErrorNumber purpose "ERANGE: a result past what its type holds"
rangeErrorNumber type Int32
rangeErrorNumber value 34

alnumBit is constant
alnumBit purpose "isalnum's class bit"
alnumBit type Int64
alnumBit value 8

